#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""merge-check (sf#1207): classify a reviewed PR under the merge rules.

Usage: merge-check <owner/repo> <pr-number> <head-sha40> [--base-url URL]

Env: FORGEJO_TOKEN (header only); FORGEJO_API_URL when --base-url is absent;
  PAPERCLIP_API_URL, PAPERCLIP_API_KEY (header only), PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID;
  TYPESAFE_API_KEY or JEV_API_KEY (header only; absent is no Jev signal),
  JEV_API_URL (tests only); FLEET_STATE_DIR (default ~/.local/state/fleet);
  FACTORYIGNORE_CLI (tests only; default the forge-pr plugin's factoryignore-cli.js).
Output: JSON {class: "A"|"B"|"C"|"stale", mergeable: bool, checks, smythe, jev, reasons}.
  stale: PR merged/closed, or the live head is not <head-sha40>.
  C: a client/* repo, before anything else and with no Forge or board read: client
     is off-limits until it moves from GitHub (sf#1375), except client/client-agent,
     which has moved to Forge (Rico, 2026-10-06). Otherwise the review
     lead's verdict for this head is fix-first or absent, or a
     required status is not success. checks says which: "red" (failure/error)
     or "pending" (missing or not finished). Required is factory/infra-static
     for a repo enrolled `checks: static-only` in the factory's config/repos.yml
     on main (SOF-2594), the OWN_CI contexts for a repo that runs its own CI
     (sf#1400: rtech/k3s-deploy; rtech/rtech-whisper; rodaddy/mcp2cli), and factory/prepush,
     factory/pr-review for every other repo. Also, on every repo and whoever opened it (sf#1413),
     a PR body with no real `## Backout` or `## Test plan` section, or a big
     change whose Backout carries no `rehearsed: <url>` line; and (sf#1482)
     a body missing Development's PR-body set, named by its first missing item.
     A PR whose base is not the repo's default branch (a stacked child, sf#1911)
     is class C until its parent lands and it is retargeted; a PR with no base
     on Forge is class C `base branch unknown`.
  B: Rico's class (sf#1375, narrowed by sf#1493): label needs-rico, which only
     Rico applies; or (sf#1690) a diff whose removed lines (the old side of an
     edit included) cite Rico with a date or ruling, or `(Rico`: reason
     `changes a Rico ruling: <file>:<old line>: <text>`. Binary changes also need Rico. Undoing a ruling stays with Rico
     (company-conduct, "Rico only"). Added lines citing Rico are fine. A diff
     that cannot be read is class C `could not read the diff for the ruling check`.
  checks: "green"/"red"/"pending" over the factory/* statuses; "repo-ci" when
     the head has no factory/* status and every status it has is success (the
     repo's own CI meets the requirement; a failing or pending one is "red" or
     "pending", class C); "none" when the head has no status at all: class C,
     reason `smythe review: ...`, until Smythe decides.
  A: everything else; the only class with mergeable true.
  smythe: null, or {decision: approve|kickback|pending, reason, override}.
  jev: Jev merge-go's probability for this head, or null when not asked.

Smythe decides (Rico, 2026-10-06). A verdict line counts from Smythe or the Review
Lead he dispatched (SOF-8387, below), the latest authorized one at this head
winning. A head with no status,
a SMYTHE_REPOS repo, or any Smythe decision line waits on Smythe, Head of
Review: class C `smythe review: <why>` until his newest line on the review issue,
in a comment under the `## Review of ... at <sha7>` heading for this head, says `smythe: approve` (class A, `smythe approved`) or `smythe:
kickback: <why>` (class C, `kickback: <why>`, back to the author). After the
kickback, a Forge PR comment whose first line starts `just do it`, posted at or
after it by the PR's author or rodaddy, is class A `override by <login>`; any
other login is ignored. needs-rico (class B) is unchanged.

Otherwise a lead's approve asks Jev merge-go (fleet/skills/merge-pr/merge-go.json):
GO (p >= 0.60, confident) is class A `... jev merge-go <p>`; no, unsure or no
signal is class C `smythe review: jev merge-go <p or no signal>`, Smythe's as
above. Every override is appended once (repo, number, head) to
$FLEET_STATE_DIR/merge-go-precedents.jsonl; Jev's state carries the repo's ten
newest as `precedents`, and bin/precedents-harvest prints them as examples.

The verdict is read from the BOARD, never from Forge: the latest verdict comment
on the issue `Review <owner/repo>#<n> @ <sha7>` whose description names
<head-sha40>, written by an authorized author. The board stamps the author, so a
comment by anyone else, on either side, cannot supply or override it. The
authorized authors (SOF-8387):
  Smythe, Head of Review: always, as before (legacy and countersigned reviews).
  The Review Lead Smythe dispatched for THIS review issue: Adams or Czajka.
    A dispatch is Smythe's own act on that issue (review-dispatch step 2):
    his comment `Dispatched to <lead> (<k> open) per review-dispatch`, or his
    assignment of the issue to the lead in the board's activity log (actor
    stamp agent Smythe). The lead's verdict counts only when posted after that
    dispatch and before Smythe's next one. A dispatch naming anyone else (an
    assignment to a non-lead included), a dispatch comment naming two leads,
    or two dispatches at one instant naming different agents authorize nobody
    and end the earlier window; a lead name held by no agent or by two
    authorizes nobody. A dispatch line, or an assignment, by anyone but Smythe
    is ignored.
The latest authorized verdict wins. A dispatched lead's `escalate: <why>` line
(or a legacy `council call: <why>` from that lead, read the same) in its window hands the decision to Smythe: class C `smythe review: <why>` until
Smythe answers after the latest such line, and then only his answers after it
count: his own verdict, or exactly `smythe: approve` (as approve) or
`smythe: kickback: <why>` (class C `kickback: <why>`). A `smythe:` line with no
escalate before it decides no verdict; under this head's review heading it is
still Smythe's decision above. Smythe's own `escalate: <why>`, or his legacy
`council call: <why>`, is an escalate too: held for his answer after it, as above.

No lead verdict (sf#1730; Rico, 2026-10-07). When pair tasks `Review
<owner/repo>#<n> @ <sha7> (<Name>)` exist for the head, pair_verdict decides in
place of a lead: the newest verdict from each family (CLAUDE_REVIEWERS,
GPT_REVIEWERS), both approve. Smythe's verdict on the head, newer than the
pair's, still wins; a legacy parent with no pair tasks drains as above.
A pair task counts when the forge-pr plugin filed it (originKind) or Smythe
did (the board's createdByAgentId; Rico, 2026-10-08, L-173: no leads, Smythe
files one Anthropic + one GPT reviewer per slice).
Each reviewer proves the PR body's `Blast radius:` line with `blast radius:
confirmed` or `blast radius: wrong: <why>` in the verdict comment (R1, L-166):
`wrong` is fix-first, and a pair approve with both confirmed is class A with no
Jev call. A pair approve missing either line still asks Jev merge-go.

Scripted non-code approve (sf#1730 US-002): with no verdict and nothing held on
the board for the head, merge-check runs factoryignore-cli for that exact head.
Only its exit 0 with `nonCode: true` and no refused path is an approve, class A
`scripted: non-code`, after every other gate (PR body, required statuses green,
needs-rico, Smythe). The Forge `verdict: approve (scripted: non-code)` comment is
never read: any CLI error, refusal or moved head leaves the old answer.
"""
import base64
import codecs
import json
from datetime import datetime, timezone
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request

REQUIRED = ["factory/prepush", "factory/pr-review"]
# A `checks: static-only` repo goes through the infra-static lane only
# (src/hooks/infra-static.ts, sf#827), which posts this one context.
REQUIRED_STATIC = ["factory/infra-static"]
# The lane is read from the enrolment on the factory's main, never from the
# statuses a head carries: anyone with write can post a status.
# A repo that runs its own Forgejo Actions CI (sf#1400) requires these contexts
# instead of the factory lanes'. The workflow is named `factory/<lane>`, so its
# native status `<workflow> / <job> (<event>)` is a factory/* status; sop-gate
# is k3s-deploy's branch-protection context, posted by the factory's lane.
OWN_CI = {
    "rtech/k3s-deploy": ["factory/k3s-ci / check (pull_request)", "sop-gate"],
    # rtech-whisper's Tests workflow, job pr-quality (rtech-whisper PR 547; Rico, 2026-10-06).
    "rtech/rtech-whisper": ["Tests / pr-quality (pull_request)"],
    # mcp2cli's CI workflow, job check (SOF-11343). It has no factory/smoke or
    # factory/prepush lane, and its factory/pr-review is advisory (config/repos.yml).
    "rodaddy/mcp2cli": ["CI / check (pull_request)"],
}
ENROLMENT = ("rodaddy/software-factory", "config/repos.yml", "main")
# Copied from jev-route SENIOR_RULES, the humanRequired entries only. These
# paths, and SMYTHE_REPOS, mark a big change for the PR-body gate (sf#1413).
# SMYTHE_REPOS also wait on Smythe's decision (Rico, 2026-10-06).
HUMAN_RULES = [
    ("secrets", re.compile(r"(auth|secret|credential|token)", re.I)),
    ("deploy", re.compile(r"(^|/)(deploy|k8s|manifests)(/|$)|^\.forgejo/workflows/", re.I)),
]
SMYTHE_REPOS = re.compile(r"^(rtech/k3s-deploy|rtech/rtech-whisper.*)$")
CLIENT = re.compile(r"^client/", re.I)
# On Forge, so merged like any repo (Rico, 2026-10-06, sf#1375).
KING_ON_FORGE = re.compile(r"client/client-agent", re.I)
VERDICT = re.compile(r"^verdict:\s*(approve-with-fixes|approve|fix-first)\s*$", re.M)
# The Head of Review (company-conduct, the crew table): his board verdict always
# counts, and he alone dispatches a review and decides an escalation (Rico,
# 2026-10-06).
LEAD_NAME = "Smythe"
# The Review Leads Smythe dispatches a review to (SOF-8387). A lead's verdict
# counts only on a review issue Smythe dispatched to that lead, inside the window.
REVIEW_LEADS = ["Adams", "Czajka"]
# sf#1730 (Rico, 2026-10-07): no lead verdict. The reviewer pair's seats by
# family, resolved by NAME; the newest verdict from each family on its pair task
# `Review <repo>#<n> @ <sha7> (<Name>)`, both approve, is the go.
# Adams and Czajka are reviewers of their family on a pair task (R5, L-166) and
# stay in REVIEW_LEADS for the legacy lead path.
CLAUDE_REVIEWERS = ["Kapoor", "Giraud", "Adams"]
GPT_REVIEWERS = ["Colter", "Kong", "Czajka"]
# R1 (L-166): the reviewer's proof of the PR body's `Blast radius:` line.
# Key and value are case-insensitive (SOF-10778): a `Wrong:` objection is never
# dropped as an old-skill missing line; an unknown value still is.
BLAST = re.compile(r"^(?i:blast radius:[ \t]*(confirmed|wrong:[ \t]*(\S.*)))[ \t]*$", re.M)
# Smythe's decision under this head's review heading (Rico,
# 2026-10-06): main() reads it for a no-status head, a SMYTHE_REPOS repo, or
# any such line.
SMYTHE = re.compile(r"^smythe:\s*(approve|kickback:\s*(\S.*?))\s*$", re.M)
# After Smythe's kickback, the author or rodaddy overrides it on the Forge PR.
OVERRIDE = re.compile(r"^just do it\b", re.I)
OVERRIDERS = ["rodaddy"]
# Jev merge-go (sf#1375; Rico, 2026-10-06): the endpoint and model src/jev/client.ts
# pins, and the classifier beside the skill. realpath: install.sh runs this through
# a ~/.local/bin symlink (PR 1556 round 2).
JEV_ENDPOINT = "https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone"
JEV_MODEL = "jev-1.13.0"
MERGE_GO = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "../merge-go.json")
STATE_MAX = 1500
# Overrides Jev learns from (Rico, 2026-10-06: "put it into some sort of memory file").
PRECEDENTS = "merge-go-precedents.jsonl"
# Smythe's dispatch line (review-dispatch step 2), at the start of a line. He
# sometimes ends it with `;` or `,` and more text, so only the words are fixed.
DISPATCH = re.compile(r"^Dispatched to (\S+) \([^)\n]*\) per review-dispatch\b", re.M)
# A dispatched lead hands the decision to Smythe (the retired lead skill). After it
# his own verdict, or his decision line (review-dispatch, "Deciding a `smythe
# review:` PR"), decides. A legacy `council call: <why>` reads the same, from a
# lead or from Smythe himself (Rico, 2026-10-06: Smythe's council call is an
# escalate).
ESCALATE = re.compile(r"^(?:escalate|council call):[ \t]*(\S.*?)\s*$", re.M)
SMYTHE_SAYS = re.compile(r"^smythe:[ \t]*(approve|kickback:[ \t]*(\S.*?))\s*$", re.M)
PAGE = 50
# A pair task is one the forge-pr plugin filed (the host stamps its originKind)
# or one Smythe created (the board's createdByAgentId, L-173). A former lead's
# child review tasks share the `(<Name>)` title but are `manual` and not his.
PAIR_ORIGIN = "plugin:rodaddy.forge-pr"

# The non-code re-derivation beside the classifier (sf#1730 US-002).
FACTORYIGNORE_CLI = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)),
                                 "../../../plugins/forge-pr/factoryignore-cli.js")
# The PR-body gate (sf#1413; Rico, 2026-10-05: "Any PR that doesn't have a back
# out plan and a test plan gets denied hard"): the two section headings, the
# line that ends a section, the filler that counts as no section, and the
# rehearsal link a big change's Backout must carry.
BACKOUT_HEAD = re.compile(r"^#{2,3}\s+(backout|back\s+out)(\s+plan)?\s*$", re.I)
TEST_PLAN_HEAD = re.compile(r"^#{2,3}\s+test\s+plan\s*$", re.I)
SECTION_END = re.compile(r"^#{1,3}\s")
# An unclosed comment runs to the end of the body, as a renderer shows it.
HTML_COMMENT = re.compile(r"<!--.*?(?:-->|\Z)", re.S)
FILLER = {"tbd", "todo", "n/a", "na", "none", "later", "will test later", "-"}
REHEARSED = re.compile(r"^\s*rehearsed:\s*https?://\S+", re.I | re.M)
# Development's PR-body set (sf#1482): the signature first line, the Summary,
# Evidence and Merge danger headings, the door words and Blast radius line the
# Merge danger section must carry, and the issue link.
SIGNATURE = re.compile(r"^\*\*agent:\*\* ")
SUMMARY_HEAD = re.compile(r"^#{2,3}\s+summary\s*$", re.I)
EVIDENCE_HEAD = re.compile(r"^#{2,3}\s+evidence\s*$", re.I)
MERGE_DANGER_HEAD = re.compile(r"^#{2,3}\s+merge\s+danger\s*$", re.I)
DOOR = re.compile(r"\b(two|one)-way door\b", re.I)
BLAST_RADIUS = re.compile(r"^Blast radius:", re.M)
ISSUE_LINK = re.compile(r"/issues/\d+\b")


def die(msg, code=2):
    sys.stderr.write(f"merge-check: {msg}\n")
    sys.exit(code)


def get(api, token, path, scheme="token", who="forge"):
    req = urllib.request.Request(api + path, headers={"Authorization": f"{scheme} {token}", "Accept": "application/json"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=20) as r:
            return json.loads(r.read().decode())
    except Exception as e:  # never echo the token or the body
        die(f"{who} GET {path.split('?')[0]} failed: {type(e).__name__}")


def get_text(api, token, path):
    """<path> on Forge as text, or None when the read fails. Never fatal, never echoes the token."""
    req = urllib.request.Request(api + path, headers={"Authorization": f"token {token}"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=20) as r:
            return r.read().decode("utf-8", "replace")
    except Exception:
        return None


def git_path(raw):
    """Decode Git's C-quoted UTF-8 path before stripping its side prefix."""
    if raw.startswith('"') and raw.endswith('"'):
        raw = codecs.escape_decode(raw[1:-1].encode())[0].decode("utf-8", "replace")
    return raw[2:] if raw.startswith(("a/", "b/")) else raw


def ruling_removed(diff):
    """Track old hunk lines; header syntax is metadata only before a hunk."""
    path, old_line = "", None
    for ln in diff.split("\n"):
        ln = ln.removesuffix("\r")
        if ln.startswith("diff --git "):
            header = re.match(r'("(?:\\.|[^"\\])*"|a/.*?) (?:"b/|b/)', ln[11:])
            path = git_path(header.group(1)) if header else "unknown path"
            old_line = None
            continue
        if ln.startswith("@@"):
            header = re.match(r"@@ -(\d+)(?:,\d+)? \+\d+(?:,\d+)? @@", ln)
            if not header:
                return f"diff for {path} cannot be checked for ruling lines"
            old_line = int(header.group(1))
            continue
        if old_line is None and (ln.startswith("Binary files ") or ln == "GIT binary patch"):
            return f"binary change to {path} cannot be checked for ruling lines"
        if old_line is None and ln.startswith("--- "):
            path = git_path(ln[4:])
            continue
        if old_line is None:
            continue
        if ln.startswith("-") and re.search(r"(?i)\brico\b", ln):
            return f"changes a Rico ruling: {path}:{old_line}: {ln[1:].strip()[:80]}"
        if ln.startswith(("-", " ")):
            old_line += 1
    return None


def get_pr_files(api, token, path):
    """Complete structured file list, or None on any unreadable page."""
    out = []
    for page in range(1, 101):
        raw = get_text(api, token, f"{path}?limit={PAGE}&page={page}")
        try:
            items = json.loads(raw)
        except (TypeError, ValueError):
            return None
        if not isinstance(items, list) or any(
                not isinstance(f, dict) or not isinstance(f.get("filename"), str) or not f["filename"]
                or (f.get("previous_filename") is not None and not isinstance(f["previous_filename"], str))
                for f in items):
            return None
        out.extend(items)
        if len(items) < PAGE:
            return out
    return None


def protected_file(path):
    return path in ("_DOCS/decisions.md", "_DOCS/decisions-ledger.md") or path.rsplit("/", 1)[-1] == "AGENTS.md"


def get_all(api, token, path):
    out = []
    for page in range(1, 101):
        items = get(api, token, f"{path}?limit={PAGE}&page={page}")
        if not isinstance(items, list):
            break
        out.extend(items)
        if len(items) < PAGE:
            break
    return out


def enrolled_checks(api, token, repo):
    """The `checks:` value config/repos.yml gives <repo>; "standard" when unlisted.

    No YAML library on the box, so this reads the one shape the file uses: the
    top-level `repositories:` list, each item opened by `  -` and holding keys at
    four spaces. Every `  -` opens a new item and name/checks are read in any
    order, so one item's lane can never land on another (SOF-2653).
    """
    owner_repo, path, ref = ENROLMENT
    doc = get(api, token, f"/repos/{owner_repo}/contents/{path}?ref={ref}")
    try:
        text = base64.b64decode(doc.get("content") or "").decode()
    except Exception as e:
        die(f"{path} on {owner_repo}@{ref} is not readable: {type(e).__name__}")
    lines = text.splitlines()
    if "repositories:" not in (ln.split("#")[0].rstrip() for ln in lines):
        die(f"{path} on {owner_repo}@{ref} has no repositories: list")
    inside, item, items = False, None, []
    for ln in lines:
        bare = ln.split("#")[0].rstrip()
        if not bare:
            continue
        if not bare[0].isspace():
            inside, item = bare == "repositories:", None
            continue
        if not inside:
            continue
        start = re.fullmatch(r"  -(?: (.*))?", bare)
        if start:
            item, body = {}, start.group(1) or ""
            items.append(item)
        elif item is not None and re.match(r"    \S", bare):
            body = bare[4:]
        else:
            continue
        kv = re.fullmatch(r"(name|checks):\s*[\"']?([\w./-]+)[\"']?", body)
        if kv:
            item[kv.group(1)] = kv.group(2)
    found = None
    for it in items:
        if it.get("name") == repo:
            found = it.get("checks")
    return found or "standard"


def body_section(body, head):
    """The content under the first <head> line of <body>, or None when it is missing.

    HTML comments are dropped from the whole body first (an unclosed one runs to
    the end), so a heading or content a renderer hides is not there. A section
    runs to the next `#`..`###` heading or the end of the body, and content that
    is only filler (TBD, n/a, ...) is no section at all.
    """
    lines = HTML_COMMENT.sub("", body or "").splitlines()
    for i, ln in enumerate(lines):
        if not head.match(ln):
            continue
        rest = []
        for nxt in lines[i + 1:]:
            if SECTION_END.match(nxt):
                break
            rest.append(nxt)
        text = "\n".join(rest).strip()
        # A bare "-" strips to nothing, so an empty remainder is filler too.
        norm = text.lower().strip(".:- \t\r\n")
        if not norm or norm in FILLER:
            return None
        return text
    return None


def body_set_missing(body):
    """The first item of Development's PR-body set (sf#1482) <body> lacks, else None.

    Order: the `**agent:** ` signature as the first visible line, `## Summary`,
    `## Evidence`, `## Merge danger` with `two-way door` or `one-way door` and
    a line starting `Blast radius:`, then an `/issues/<n>` link. Hidden HTML
    comments do not count, as in body_section.
    """
    visible = HTML_COMMENT.sub("", body or "")
    first = next((ln.strip() for ln in visible.splitlines() if ln.strip()), "")
    if not SIGNATURE.match(first):
        return "missing **agent:** signature first line"
    if body_section(body, SUMMARY_HEAD) is None:
        return "missing ## Summary"
    if body_section(body, EVIDENCE_HEAD) is None:
        return "missing ## Evidence"
    danger = body_section(body, MERGE_DANGER_HEAD)
    if danger is None:
        return "missing ## Merge danger"
    if not DOOR.search(danger):
        return "missing two-way door or one-way door in merge danger"
    if not BLAST_RADIUS.search(danger):
        return "missing Blast radius: line in merge danger"
    if not ISSUE_LINK.search(visible):
        return "missing /issues/<n> link"
    return None


def when(stamp):
    """<stamp> (ISO 8601 with an offset, board or Forge) as an aware datetime, else None."""
    try:
        t = datetime.fromisoformat(str(stamp).replace("Z", "+00:00"))
    except ValueError:
        return None
    return t if t.tzinfo else None


def override_by(api, token, repo, num, since, author):
    """The first login among <author> and OVERRIDERS whose Forge PR comment opens
    with `just do it` at or after <since> (Smythe's kickback), else None."""
    since, allowed = when(since), {author, *OVERRIDERS} - {""}
    if since is None:
        return None
    for c in get_all(api, token, f"/repos/{repo}/issues/{num}/comments"):
        login = (c.get("user") or {}).get("login") or ""
        at = when(c.get("created_at") or "")
        first = (c.get("body") or "").split("\n", 1)[0].strip()
        if login in allowed and at is not None and at >= since and OVERRIDE.match(first):
            return login
    return None


def dispatched(dispatches, at):
    """The agent id Smythe's latest dispatch before <at> authorizes, or None.

    <dispatches> is [(at, agent id or None)] on one review issue. The latest
    dispatch at or before <at> decides; one at <at> itself authorizes nobody (the
    verdict must come after it), so a redispatch at the verdict's own instant
    ends the earlier window. Two dispatches at the latest instant naming
    different agents authorize nobody.
    """
    before = [d for d in dispatches if d[0] <= at]
    if not before:
        return None
    last = max(d[0] for d in before)
    if last == at:
        return None
    targets = {d[1] for d in before if d[0] == last}
    return targets.pop() if len(targets) == 1 else None


def decide(events, escalates):
    """(verdict or None, held reason or None) from one head's authorized events.

    <events> is [(at, who, verdict, why)]: who is "smythe", "lead" or
    "decision" (Smythe's `smythe: approve|kickback: <why>` line). The latest
    event wins. A decision line counts only after the latest `escalate: <why>`,
    a dispatched lead's or Smythe's own (<escalates> is [(at, why)]), and after
    that escalate only
    Smythe's later events count; with none the PR is held for him.
    """
    if escalates:
        at, why = max(escalates)
        events = [e for e in events if e[1] != "lead" and e[0] > at]
        if not events:
            return None, f"smythe review: {why}"
    else:
        events = [e for e in events if e[1] != "decision"]
    if not events:
        return None, None
    _, _, verdict, why = max(events)
    if verdict == "kickback":
        return None, f"kickback: {why}"
    return verdict, None


def lead_verdict(board, key, company, repo, num, sha, escalates=(), pair=False):
    """(the authorized verdict for exactly this head or None, events).

    The verdict is Smythe's or the dispatched Review Lead's, the latest
    (decide). The events are held, `smythe review: <why>` while an escalation
    (a dispatched lead's, or Smythe's own `escalate:` or legacy `council call:`)
    waits on Smythe or `kickback: <why>` when he kicked it back, or None;
    smythe, his newest (at, approve|kickback, why) decision line under this
    head's review heading, or None; and review, the newest authorized verdict
    comment's body.

    sf#1730: <escalates> are the reviewer pair's [(at, why)], held for Smythe
    as a lead's are; with <pair> (pair tasks exist for this head) no lead's
    verdict counts. ev["smythe_at"] is Smythe's newest event on this head.
    """

    def bget(path):
        return get(board, key, path, scheme="Bearer", who="board")

    agents = bget(f"/api/companies/{company}/agents")
    leads = [a.get("id") for a in agents if a.get("name") == LEAD_NAME and a.get("id")] if isinstance(agents, list) else []
    if len(leads) != 1:
        die(f"board has {len(leads)} agents named {LEAD_NAME}, need exactly 1")
    # A Review Lead is the one agent of that name; a name held by none or by two
    # can be dispatched nothing (SOF-8387).
    lead_of = {}
    for name in REVIEW_LEADS:
        ids = [a.get("id") for a in agents if a.get("name") == name and a.get("id")]
        lead_of[name] = ids[0] if len(ids) == 1 else None
    lead_ids = {i for i in lead_of.values() if i}
    decisions = []
    title = f"Review {repo}#{num} @ {sha[:7]}"
    # The lead's heading, bare or with the PR linked as company-conduct asks:
    # `## Review of owner/repo#n at sha7` or `## Review of [owner/repo#n](url) at sha7`.
    ref = re.escape(f"{repo}#{num}")
    heading = re.compile(rf"^## Review of (?:{ref}|\[{ref}\]\([^)\s]*\)) at {sha[:7]}\s*$", re.M)
    issues = bget(f"/api/companies/{company}/issues?q={urllib.parse.quote(title)}&limit={PAGE}")
    events, handed, reviewed = [], list(escalates), []
    for issue in issues if isinstance(issues, list) else []:
        # Bound to the full head: the 7 characters in the title are not enough.
        if issue.get("title") != title or sha not in (issue.get("description") or ""):
            continue
        comments = bget(f"/api/issues/{urllib.parse.quote(str(issue.get('id')), safe='')}/comments")
        comments = [c for c in comments if isinstance(c, dict)] if isinstance(comments, list) else []
        # Smythe's dispatches on THIS issue: who each one authorizes. A comment
        # naming two leads, or anyone not a Review Lead, authorizes nobody.
        dispatches = []
        for c in comments:
            if c.get("authorAgentId") != leads[0]:
                continue
            named = set(DISPATCH.findall(c.get("body") or ""))
            if named:
                one = named.pop() if len(named) == 1 else None
                dispatches.append((c.get("createdAt") or "", lead_of.get(one) if one else None))
        # His assignment of the issue to a Review Lead is the same dispatch
        # (review-dispatch step 2), from the board's activity log: actorType and
        # actorId are the board's stamp, never a comment's text. A move to anyone
        # else ends the window as a dispatch to a non-lead does.
        if lead_ids:
            iid = urllib.parse.quote(str(issue.get("id")), safe="")
            acts = bget(f"/api/issues/{iid}/activity")
            for a in acts if isinstance(acts, list) else []:
                moved = (((a.get("details") or {}).get("changes") or {}).get("assigneeAgentId")
                         if isinstance(a, dict) and a.get("action") == "issue.updated" else None)
                if (isinstance(moved, dict) and a.get("actorType") == "agent"
                        and a.get("actorId") == leads[0] and a.get("createdAt")):
                    to = moved.get("to")
                    dispatches.append((a["createdAt"], to if to in lead_ids else None))
        for c in comments:
            body, who, at = c.get("body") or "", c.get("authorAgentId"), c.get("createdAt") or ""
            # Smythe's verdict always counts; a Review Lead's only inside its dispatch.
            lead = not pair and who != leads[0] and who is not None and dispatched(dispatches, at) == who
            # A dispatched lead's escalate hands the decision to Smythe; Smythe's own
            # `escalate:` or legacy `council call:` line is the same escalate (Rico,
            # 2026-10-06), held until he answers after it.
            if (lead or who == leads[0]) and ESCALATE.findall(body):
                handed.append((at, ESCALATE.findall(body)[-1]))
            if who == leads[0] and SMYTHE_SAYS.findall(body):
                word, why = SMYTHE_SAYS.findall(body)[-1]
                events.append((at, "decision", "approve" if word == "approve" else "kickback", why))
            if who == leads[0]:
                # A decision counts only under the review heading naming this
                # head: another head's approve or kickback decides nothing here.
                said = SMYTHE.findall(body) if heading.search(body) else []
                if said:
                    word, why = said[-1]
                    decisions.append((at, "approve" if word == "approve" else "kickback", why or None))
            if (who != leads[0] and not lead) or not heading.search(body):
                continue
            lines = VERDICT.findall(body)
            if lines:
                events.append((at, "smythe" if who == leads[0] else "lead", lines[-1], None))
                # The review Jev merge-go reads: the newest authorized verdict comment.
                reviewed.append((at, body))
    verdict, held = decide(events, handed)
    ev = {"held": held, "smythe": max(decisions) if decisions else None,
          "review": max(reviewed)[1] if reviewed else ""}
    # Smythe's own: his verdicts and decision lines, and the escalates after the
    # seeded ones (a lead's count only without a pair, where this is unused).
    ev["answered"] = max([e[0] for e in events if e[1] != "lead"], default="")
    ev["smythe_at"] = max([ev["answered"]] + [d[0] for d in decisions]
                          + [h[0] for h in handed[len(escalates):]], default="")
    return verdict, ev


def pair_verdict(board, key, company, repo, num, sha, author=""):
    """(approve|fix-first|pending|escalated, ev) from the reviewer pair on this head (sf#1730).

    A pair task binds to the head by its exact title `Review <repo>#<n> @ <sha7>
    (<Name>)` and the full <sha> in its description, and is one forge-pr filed
    (originKind PAIR_ORIGIN) or Smythe filed (createdByAgentId, L-173): a lead's
    own child tasks carry the same title. A comment counts only by the
    board's stamp authorAgentId, held by a seat in exactly one family and not the
    PR author's own seat (<author> is the Forge login, `sf-<name>`), under this
    head's review heading. Per family the newest verdict wins, a tie going to
    fix-first; approve-with-fixes is fix-first. Any fix-first is fix-first, both
    approve is approve, else pending. A reviewer's `escalate:` (or `council
    call:`) line is escalated, for Smythe. Forge is never read.
    Smythe files a pair per slice (L-173), so every exact-head task counts
    on its own regardless of status: any task's newest fix-first is fix-first,
    any task without a verdict is pending unless cancelled, whatever another
    slice's task of that family said.
    """

    def bget(path):
        return get(board, key, path, scheme="Bearer", who="board")

    agents = bget(f"/api/companies/{company}/agents")
    agents = [a for a in agents if isinstance(a, dict)] if isinstance(agents, list) else []
    own = author[3:].lower() if author.startswith("sf-") else None

    def seats(names):
        out = set()
        for name in names:
            ids = [a.get("id") for a in agents if a.get("name") == name and a.get("id")]
            out |= set(ids) if len(ids) == 1 else set()
        return out - {a.get("id") for a in agents if own and str(a.get("name") or "").lower() == own}

    fams = {"claude": seats(CLAUDE_REVIEWERS), "gpt": seats(GPT_REVIEWERS)}
    # The Head of Review's agent id, when exactly one agent holds the name.
    heads = [a.get("id") for a in agents if a.get("name") == LEAD_NAME and a.get("id")]
    head = heads[0] if len(heads) == 1 else None
    stem = f"Review {repo}#{num} @ {sha[:7]} ("
    titles = {f"{stem}{n})" for n in CLAUDE_REVIEWERS + GPT_REVIEWERS}
    ref = re.escape(f"{repo}#{num}")
    heading = re.compile(rf"^## Review of (?:{ref}|\[{ref}\]\([^)\s]*\)) at {sha[:7]}\s*$", re.M)
    issues = bget(f"/api/companies/{company}/issues?q={urllib.parse.quote(stem)}&limit={PAGE}")
    tasks, said, handed, by_task, blast_by_task = 0, {"claude": [], "gpt": []}, [], {}, {}
    for issue in issues if isinstance(issues, list) else []:
        if not isinstance(issue, dict) or issue.get("title") not in titles or sha not in (issue.get("description") or ""):
            continue
        # Filed by the forge-pr plugin, or by Smythe himself (review-dispatch
        # step 3; Rico, 2026-10-08, L-173): the board's creator stamp, never text.
        if issue.get("originKind") != PAIR_ORIGIN and not (head and issue.get("createdByAgentId") == head):
            continue
        # Read verdicts before status: cancellation never removes evidence.
        mine = []
        comments = bget(f"/api/issues/{urllib.parse.quote(str(issue.get('id')), safe='')}/comments")
        for c in comments if isinstance(comments, list) else []:
            if not isinstance(c, dict):
                continue
            body, who, at = str(c.get("body") or ""), c.get("authorAgentId"), str(c.get("createdAt") or "")
            fam = [f for f, ids in fams.items() if who in ids]
            if len(fam) != 1:
                continue
            if ESCALATE.findall(body):
                handed.append((at, ESCALATE.findall(body)[-1]))
            lines = VERDICT.findall(body) if heading.search(body) else []
            if lines:
                # R1: the last blast-radius line of the same comment; `wrong` is fix-first.
                blast = BLAST.findall(body)
                b = ("wrong" if blast[-1][1] else "confirmed") if blast else ""
                v = "approve" if lines[-1] == "approve" and b != "wrong" else "fix-first"
                said[fam[0]].append((at, v == "fix-first", v, body, b))
                mine.append((at, v == "fix-first", v, b))
        if not mine and issue.get("status") == "cancelled":
            continue
        tasks += 1
        tid = str(issue.get("identifier") or issue.get("id"))
        by_task[tid] = max(mine)[2] if mine else None
        blast_by_task[tid] = (max(mine)[3] or None) if mine else None
    newest = {f: max(vs) if vs else None for f, vs in said.items()}
    return pair_state(newest, handed, tasks, by_task=by_task, blast_by_task=blast_by_task)


def pair_state(newest, handed, tasks, answered="", by_task=None, blast_by_task=None):
    """pair_verdict's (state, ev) from each family's newest verdict and the escalates.

    An escalate Smythe answered (an event of his strictly after it, <answered>
    being his newest, lead_verdict's ev["answered"]) is resolved and dropped, so
    a later pair comment never reopens it. ev["escalates"] keeps all of them,
    for lead_verdict to weigh against his answers. <by_task> ({task: its newest
    verdict or None}, L-173) decides per task when given; None keeps the
    per-family rule. <blast_by_task> ({task: its newest verdict's blast or None})
    is carried in ev for R1.
    """
    escalates, handed = handed, [h for h in handed if h[0] >= answered]
    missing = [f for f, v in newest.items() if v is None]
    if by_task is not None and not missing:
        missing = [t for t, v in by_task.items() if v is None]
    if by_task is None:
        fixes = any(v and v[2] == "fix-first" for v in newest.values())
    else:
        fixes = "fix-first" in by_task.values()
    if handed:
        state = "escalated"
    elif fixes:
        state = "fix-first"
    else:
        state = "pending" if missing else "approve"
    counted = [v for v in newest.values() if v]
    ev = {"held": f"smythe review: {max(handed)[1]}" if handed else None, "smythe": None,
          "review": max(counted)[3] if counted else "", "missing": missing, "tasks": tasks, "escalates": escalates,
          "at": max([v[0] for v in counted] + [h[0] for h in handed], default=""), "newest": newest,
          "by_task": by_task, "blast_by_task": blast_by_task}
    ev.update({f: ({"verdict": v[2], "at": v[0], "blast": v[4] or None} if v else None) for f, v in newest.items()})
    return state, ev


def review_verdict(board, key, company, repo, num, sha, login=""):
    """The merge gate's authoritative verdict, evidence and counted pair tasks."""
    state, pev = pair_verdict(board, key, company, repo, num, sha, login)
    verdict, ev = lead_verdict(board, key, company, repo, num, sha, pev["escalates"], pev["tasks"] > 0)
    if pev["tasks"]:
        # An escalate Smythe answered is resolved; a later pair comment never reopens it.
        state, pev = pair_state(pev["newest"], pev["escalates"], pev["tasks"], ev["answered"],
                                by_task=pev["by_task"], blast_by_task=pev["blast_by_task"])
    if pev["tasks"] and ev["smythe_at"] <= pev["at"]:
        # An unanswered escalate stays held whatever the pair says after it: only
        # Smythe's answer clears it, never a newer pair verdict.
        held = ev["held"] if str(ev["held"] or "").startswith("smythe review: ") else pev["held"]
        verdict, ev = (state if state in ("approve", "fix-first") else None), {**pev, "smythe": ev["smythe"], "held": held}
    return verdict, ev, pev

def scripted_non_code(api, token, repo, num, sha):
    """True only when factoryignore-cli exits 0 for <sha> with nonCode true and
    nothing refused (sf#1730 US-002). Anything else, a failure included, is False."""
    cli = os.environ.get("FACTORYIGNORE_CLI") or FACTORYIGNORE_CLI
    env = {**os.environ, "FORGEJO_API_URL": api, "FORGEJO_TOKEN": token}
    try:
        p = subprocess.run([cli, repo, num, sha], env=env, capture_output=True, timeout=120)
        if p.returncode != 0:
            return False
        v = json.loads(p.stdout.decode().strip())
    except Exception:  # never echo the token or the output
        return False
    return isinstance(v, dict) and v.get("nonCode") is True and v.get("refused") == []


def precedents_file():
    base = os.environ.get("FLEET_STATE_DIR") or os.path.expanduser("~/.local/state/fleet")
    return os.path.join(base, PRECEDENTS)


def read_precedents(repo):
    """Every precedent line for <repo>, oldest first; unreadable lines are skipped."""
    rows = []
    try:
        with open(precedents_file()) as f:
            for ln in f:
                try:
                    rows.append(json.loads(ln))
                except ValueError:
                    continue
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return []
    return [r for r in rows if isinstance(r, dict) and r.get("repo") == repo]


def record_precedent(row):
    """Append <row> once per (repo, number, head). A failure is logged, never fatal."""
    path = precedents_file()
    if any(r.get("number") == row["number"] and r.get("head") == row["head"] for r in read_precedents(row["repo"])):
        return
    try:
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)
        with open(path, "a") as f:
            f.write(json.dumps(row) + "\n")
    except OSError as e:
        sys.stderr.write(f"merge-check: precedent not written to {path}: {type(e).__name__}\n")


def ask_merge_go(state):
    """(p, GO?) from Jev merge-go for <state>, or (None, False) on no signal.

    NO SIGNAL IS NEVER A PASS (src/jev/client.ts). GO is the classifier's yes
    (p >= 0.5) at its `confident` threshold; unsure is not GO. The key goes in
    the header only and is never echoed.
    """
    key = os.environ.get("TYPESAFE_API_KEY") or os.environ.get("JEV_API_KEY") or ""
    try:
        with open(MERGE_GO) as f:
            clf = json.load(f)
        if not key:
            return None, False
        q = {"type": "noul", "instructions": clf["ask"]}
        body = json.dumps({"model": JEV_MODEL, "state": state, "questions": {clf["id"]: q}}).encode()
        req = urllib.request.Request(os.environ.get("JEV_API_URL") or JEV_ENDPOINT, data=body, method="POST",
                                     headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {key}", "Content-Type": "application/json"})
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=20) as r:
            a = json.loads(r.read().decode())["answers"][clf["id"]]
        p = a.get("noul") if isinstance(a, dict) else None
        if isinstance(p, bool) or not isinstance(p, (int, float)) or not 0 <= p <= 1:
            return None, False
        return float(p), p >= 0.5 and max(p, 1 - p) >= float(clf["confident"])
    except Exception:  # never echo the key, the state or the body
        return None, False


def main(argv):
    pos, base, i = [], None, 0
    while i < len(argv):
        if argv[i] == "--base-url":
            if i + 1 >= len(argv):
                die("--base-url needs a value")
            base, i = argv[i + 1], i + 2
            continue
        if argv[i].startswith("--"):
            die(f"unknown flag {argv[i]}")
        pos.append(argv[i])
        i += 1
    if (len(pos) != 3 or not re.fullmatch(r"[\w.-]+/[\w.-]+", pos[0]) or not pos[1].isdigit()
            or not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{40}", pos[2])):
        die("usage: merge-check <owner/repo> <pr-number> <head-sha40> [--base-url URL]")
    repo, num, sha = pos
    # client/* first, before any read of Forge or the board (sf#1375).
    if CLIENT.match(repo) and not KING_ON_FORGE.fullmatch(repo):
        print(json.dumps({"class": "C", "mergeable": False, "checks": None,
                          "reasons": ["client repos are off-limits until they move from GitHub (sf#1375)"]}))
        return
    api =(base or os.environ.get("FORGEJO_API_URL", "")).rstrip("/")
    token = os.environ.get("FORGEJO_TOKEN", "")
    if not api or not token:
        die("--base-url (or FORGEJO_API_URL) and FORGEJO_TOKEN are required")
    board = os.environ.get("PAPERCLIP_API_URL", "").rstrip("/")
    key = os.environ.get("PAPERCLIP_API_KEY", "")
    company = os.environ.get("PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID", "")
    if not board or not key or not re.fullmatch(r"[\w-]+", company):
        die("PAPERCLIP_API_URL, PAPERCLIP_API_KEY and PAPERCLIP_COMPANY_ID are required")

    def out(cls, reasons, checks=None, smythe=None, jev=None):
        print(json.dumps({"class": cls, "mergeable": cls == "A", "checks": checks,
                          "smythe": smythe, "jev": jev, "reasons": reasons}))

    pr = get(api, token, f"/repos/{repo}/pulls/{num}")
    live = (pr.get("head") or {}).get("sha", "")
    if pr.get("merged") or pr.get("state") != "open":
        return out("stale", [f"PR is {'merged' if pr.get('merged') else pr.get('state')}"])
    if live != sha:
        return out("stale", [f"head moved: live {live[:7]} != {sha[:7]}"])
    # sf#1911: a stacked child merges into its parent branch, not the default
    # (rtech-consulting#909 landed in its parent). Class C until the parent lands
    # and the child is retargeted; no base on Forge fails closed. The verdict and
    # status reasons below still run, so the list is complete.
    ref = (pr.get("base") or {}).get("ref")
    default = ((pr.get("base") or {}).get("repo") or {}).get("default_branch")
    stacked = []
    if not ref or not default:
        stacked.append("base branch unknown")
    elif ref != default:
        stacked.append(f"stacked: base {ref} is not the default branch {default}; land the parent, then retarget")

    # Both sides of a rename: Forge reports the old path as previous_filename
    # (probed on rodaddy/software-factory pulls 380 and 411, status "renamed").
    names, paths = [], []
    files = get_pr_files(api, token, f"/repos/{repo}/pulls/{num}/files")
    for f in files or []:
        names.extend(n for n in (f.get("filename"), f.get("previous_filename")) if n)
        paths.append({"path": f.get("filename"), "add": f.get("additions"), "del": f.get("deletions")})
    sized = lambda ps: "\n".join(f"{p.get('path')} +{p.get('add', '?')} -{p.get('del', '?')}" for p in ps)
    # The PR-body gate (sf#1413; Rico, 2026-10-05: "Any PR that doesn't have a
    # back out plan and a test plan gets denied hard"): on every repo, whoever
    # opened it, a body with no real Backout or Test plan section is class C. A
    # big change (a SMYTHE_REPOS repo, a deploy/secrets/auth/CI path, or anything but
    # markdown on rtech-infra) must also have rehearsed its backout, linked from
    # the Backout section as `rehearsed: <url>`. The verdict and status reasons
    # below still run, so the list is complete.
    backout = body_section(pr.get("body"), BACKOUT_HEAD)
    big = (bool(SMYTHE_REPOS.match(repo)) or any(rx.search(n) for _, rx in HUMAN_RULES for n in names)
           or (repo == "rtech/rtech-infra" and any(not n.endswith(".md") for n in names)))
    gate = []
    if backout is None:
        gate.append("missing backout plan")
    if body_section(pr.get("body"), TEST_PLAN_HEAD) is None:
        gate.append("missing test plan")
    if big and backout is not None and not REHEARSED.search(backout):
        gate.append("big change without a rehearsed backout")
    missing = body_set_missing(pr.get("body"))
    if missing:
        gate.append(missing)

    reasons = []
    # sf#1690: a removed line carrying a ruling is Rico's (class B, below). A
    # diff that cannot be read never makes a PR mergeable.
    diff = get_text(api, token, f"/repos/{repo}/pulls/{num}.diff")
    protected = next((n for n in names if protected_file(n)), None)
    ruling = f"change to a ruling file {protected}" if protected else ruling_removed(diff) if diff is not None else None
    if files is None:
        reasons.append("could not read the PR file list for the ruling check")
    if diff is None:
        reasons.append("could not read the diff for the ruling check")
    # The opener is Forge's stamp: the author who may override a kickback.
    login = (pr.get("user") or {}).get("login") or ""
    # sf#1730: Smythe's verdict on this head > the reviewer pair (when a pair
    # task for it exists) > a legacy parent's dispatched lead.
    verdict, ev, pev = review_verdict(board, key, company, repo, num, sha, login)

    # sf#1730 US-002: no board verdict and nothing held, so re-derive the
    # non-code fast path for this exact head. A board verdict always wins.
    scripted = verdict is None and not ev.get("smythe") and not pev["tasks"] and not ev["held"] and scripted_non_code(api, token, repo, num, sha)
    if scripted:
        verdict = "approve"
    if ev["held"]:
        reasons.append(ev["held"])
    elif verdict == "fix-first":
        reasons.append("review verdict fix-first")
    elif verdict is None and pev["tasks"]:
        reasons.append(f"pair verdict pending ({', '.join(pev['missing'])}) on {sha[:7]}")
    elif verdict is None:
        reasons.append(f"no lead verdict on the board for {sha[:7]}")
    status = get(api, token, f"/repos/{repo}/commits/{sha}/status")
    states = {s.get("context"): s.get("status") or s.get("state") for s in (status.get("statuses") or [])}
    # A head with no factory/* status is a repo the factory does not check
    # (Rico, 2026-10-06, sf#1493: agents decide, not Rico). Its own CI meets the
    # checks requirement when every status is success ("repo-ci"); a failing or
    # pending one is red or pending, exactly as a factory check. A head with no
    # status at all is Smythe's (checks "none", class C until he decides).
    # A repo in OWN_CI (sf#1400) always requires its own contexts, so a head
    # carrying only some of them is never read as "repo-ci".
    # SOF-12237: in repo CI a "skipped" job is one its own workflow chose not to
    # run on this event (a deploy gated on a push to main); it is neither red
    # nor pending, as Forgejo's combined state already reads it. At least one
    # job must still be success: a head where every status is skipped proves
    # nothing. A required factory/* or OWN_CI context is unchanged: skipped
    # there is still not success.
    own_ci = OWN_CI.get(repo)
    if not states:
        checks = "none"
    elif own_ci is None and not any(str(ctx).startswith("factory/") for ctx in states):
        checks = "repo-ci"
        if all(st == "skipped" for st in states.values()):
            reasons.append("every repo CI status is skipped")
            checks = "pending"
        for ctx, st in sorted(states.items(), key=lambda kv: str(kv[0])):
            if st not in ("success", "skipped"):
                reasons.append(f"{ctx} is {st or 'missing'}")
                if st in ("failure", "error"):
                    checks = "red"
                elif checks != "red":
                    checks = "pending"
    else:
        checks = "green"
        required = own_ci
        if required is None:
            static = enrolled_checks(api, token, repo) == "static-only"
            required = REQUIRED_STATIC if static else REQUIRED
        for ctx in required:
            if states.get(ctx) != "success":
                reasons.append(f"{ctx} is {states.get(ctx) or 'missing'}")
                if states.get(ctx) in ("failure", "error"):
                    checks = "red"
                elif checks != "red":
                    checks = "pending"
    if stacked or gate or reasons:
        return out("C", [*stacked, *gate, *reasons], checks)

    # Rico's class (sf#1375, narrowed by sf#1493): the label needs-rico, which
    # only Rico applies; or a diff that removes or edits a ruling line (sf#1690).
    if any((lb.get("name") == "needs-rico") for lb in (pr.get("labels") or [])):
        return out("B", ["label needs-rico"], checks)
    if ruling:
        return out("B", [ruling], checks)
    routine = f"verdict {verdict}; required statuses green"
    # Rico, 2026-10-06: a head with no status at all, a SMYTHE_REPOS
    # repo, or any Smythe decision line waits on Smythe. `smythe: approve` is A;
    # `smythe: kickback: <why>` is C back to the author, until the author or
    # rodaddy posts `just do it` on the Forge PR at or after the kickback.
    why = (f"{sha[:7]} carries no status" if checks == "none"
           else f"{repo} is Smythe's to review" if SMYTHE_REPOS.match(repo) else None)
    if why or ev["smythe"]:
        if ev["smythe"] is None:
            return out("C", [f"smythe review: {why}"], checks, smythe={"decision": "pending", "reason": why, "override": None})
        at, word, kick = ev["smythe"]
        if word == "approve":
            return out("A", ["smythe approved"], checks, smythe={"decision": "approve", "reason": why, "override": None})
        who = override_by(api, token, repo, num, at, login)
        s = {"decision": "kickback", "reason": kick, "override": who}
        if not who:
            return out("C", [f"kickback: {kick}"], checks, smythe=s)
        # The override is a precedent Jev reads next time (Rico, 2026-10-06).
        record_precedent({"repo": repo, "number": int(num), "head": sha, "title": str(pr.get("title") or "")[:300],
                          "paths": paths[:30], "kickback": kick, "override_by": who,
                          "at": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec="seconds")})
        return out("A", [f"override by {who}"], checks, smythe=s)
    # R1 (Rico, 2026-10-07, L-166): a pair approve whose reviewers both
    # confirmed the PR's blast radius is the go, with no Jev call.
    # L-173: with a pair per slice, every counted task's newest verdict must confirm.
    per_task = ev.get("blast_by_task")
    if (verdict == "approve" and all((ev.get(f) or {}).get("blast") == "confirmed" for f in ("claude", "gpt"))
            and (per_task is None or all(b == "confirmed" for b in per_task.values()))):
        return out("A", ["pair approve; blast radius confirmed by both"], checks)
    # sf#1730 US-002: the re-derived non-code approve, its gates above all passed.
    if scripted:
        return out("A", ["scripted: non-code"], checks)
    # A lead's approve asks Jev merge-go: GO merges; anything else is Smythe's.
    rnd = re.search(r"\*\*Round:\*\*\s*(\d+)", ev["review"])
    prior = [f"{r.get('title')} | {sized(r.get('paths') or [])} | kickback: {r.get('kickback')}"
             for r in read_precedents(repo)[-10:]]
    state = {"repo": repo, "title": str(pr.get("title") or "")[:300], "body": (pr.get("body") or "")[:STATE_MAX],
             "paths": sized(paths)[:STATE_MAX], "verdict": verdict, "round": rnd.group(1) if rnd else "1",
             "findings": ev["review"][:STATE_MAX], "checks": checks, "backout": (backout or "")[:300],
             "sensitive": "yes" if big else "no", "precedents": "\n".join(prior)[:STATE_MAX] or "none"}
    p, go = ask_merge_go(state)
    score = "no signal" if p is None else f"{p:.2f}"
    if go:
        return out("A", [f"{routine}; jev merge-go {score}"], checks, jev=p)
    return out("C", [f"smythe review: jev merge-go {score}"], checks,
               smythe={"decision": "pending", "reason": f"jev merge-go {score}", "override": None}, jev=p)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main(sys.argv[1:])
